{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791625659,"nonce":"ljtGeA95QJpIa79kQakJtVfZC1c=","title":"Serializer/Unserializer round trip of enums and class instances (Issue9484)","message":"Conformance row Issue9484 crashes \"uncompiled unit.issues.Issue9484.main\". Three bugs:\n\n1. `Unserializer.unserializeEnum\u003cT\u003e` has no annotated return type, so it infers\n   Type.createEnum's own T, foreign to the method; an argument typed by a type\n   parameter is \"uninformative\" in unify_type_args_inner, and `T` against\n   `Enum\u003cDynamic\u003e` never binds (dynamic_bound_var handles only bare T and Array\u003cT\u003e).\n   The template keeps ?T, is trap-stubbed, and unserialize/run/main cascade.\n2. Serialization is wrong even under --llvm (`cy4:Hogey1:xi-1700787760g`):\n   haxe_reflect_field (runtime/src/reflect.rs) reads a haxe_box_reference_ptr box\n   {class_tid, ptr} as the instance itself. haxe_dynamic_field unwraps such boxes;\n   haxe_reflect_field does not. Telling a box from a raw instance is ambiguous\n   without a box registry (like ARRAY_BOXES).\n3. Passing a class instance to a `{}`-typed parameter builds a fresh empty anon\n   (rayzor_ensure_shape(\"\") + rayzor_anon_new) instead of passing the object.","files":null}]}